{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128377-stat-my-criminal","id":1128377,"title":"Stat my criminal!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-13T02:57:47-07:00","id":1128377,"title":"Stat my criminal!","content":"So, for various reasons, I want/need to come up with some less savoury individuals, and since I had fun making them, wanted to see how you guys would end up doing them.<br /> So Let's create the criminals before apply Ing any sort of splat template.<br /> We would have <br /> a) the leader<br /> What qualifies a mob boss? I went the &quot;better feared than loved&quot; Route and chose Air of Menace, Striking Looks and High Presence. Intimidating is an obvious pick, as is Streetwise. However, people also need something to admire, leadership-skills. So have Expression, Inspiring, Small Unit Tactics and Cohesive Unit - he got there by being good at Showing the way and increasing Chance of survival. Allies and Status are obvious, but which would you pick? Corrupt Cops? Organized Crime?<br /> b) the Hound<br /> Someone needs to make the planning, needs to find out how to get a heist done and how to find those guys that need to pay up. Bit stumped here. Obviously high wits and int, and Investigation. Composure, since he's in the field a lot. Needs to wipe his traces, so Untouchable, Patient and good time Management. But what else?<br /> c) the Killer<br /> Someone needs to handle the violence. There are many ways here, from over brutality to snipers to stealthy murder or poisoning. What is your choice?<br /> I'd go with Lots of stealth and larceny, high dex, throw in good Weaponry and poisons via Crafts and science, as well as subterfuge and socialize. Because to me, the idea of a Killer that can strike at any time and is basically a ghost is scary.<br /> Barfly is an obvious Merit, and probably Killer Instinct. What else ? Parkour and Athletics for getting away in a cinch?<br /> d) the Bodyguard<br /> Doesn't hurt having one when you have enemies. Giant would be a good choice. Danger sense and fast reflexes. Bodyarmour would help, too. If the boss does not inspire fear, the bodyguard should.<br /> <br /> Who are you missing in this band? What do they need?<br /> Hit me up with your little mob team!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}